> But what does it mean then, if it doesn't talk about the future?  Does "pu'o
> broda" mean "a situation in which a human observer would predict that {ba
> broda}"?

Something like that, yes. After all, the truth of any claim has to be
determined by a human observer. How do you know if a claim with {mo'u}
is true or not, other than by the judgement of a human observer? When
is an event truly and well finished? Or how can you tell when a claim
with {bredi} is true? If A is ready to do B, but never does it, does
that mean that A wasn't really ready?

