In that case, he probably will catch it, since being a physicist doesn't
really prepare me for making such calls on the fly. I would trust your
instincts more than mine. :)

> I'll say {pu'o se kavbu} and you'll say {pu'o farlu}.  Are both
> statements correct?

Yes, just like if I say {le bolci cu sutra} and you say {le bolci
cu masno} both statements would be correct, in our respective opinions.
It is hard to say whether the statements are true or not. Just because
each of us believes what he is saying doesn't make it true, but what
happens in the future should not really be the deciding factor to know
whether a claim about the present is true.

